course: dictionary
lesson: 11073
title: Weirdo: rude or friendly?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can be friendly in one place and unkind in another. The context tells you which. Look at who is speaking, how they say it, and what has just happened.
explain: «Mia's chat has a "weirdo of the week" game, and in week three it's her, for a cowboy hat.» Here weirdo is part of a game, and the cowboy hat makes it sound silly and playful, not cruel.
explain: Weirdo has two meanings. The rude one means a person who seems very strange or odd. The friendly one is a joke said to a friend who does something silly. Ask yourself: is someone laughing with a friend, or pointing at someone who is not laughing?
fact: Weirdo is a slang word, so it is informal and is not used in formal writing.
fact: «Weirdo» can mean a person who seems very strange or odd, and then it is rude.
fact: «Weirdo» can also be a joke said to a friend who does something silly.
fact: Calling someone a weirdo to hurt them is bullying; the joke only works when both people are laughing.
fact: In a story, the word weirdo shows how one character sees another.
exercise: «Mia's chat has a "weirdo of the week" game, and in week three it's her, for a cowboy hat.» Is weirdo friendly or rude here? | A kind compliment about her hat | A new name for a cowboy | *A friendly joke, as part of a game | A rude insult that means she is evil
exercise: Ruby laughs and says to her best friend, «You weirdo, you ate the whole cake!» What is Ruby doing? | Reporting a crime to the police | *Joking with a friend | Saying the cake is old | Calling her friend a thief in court
exercise: A boy says loudly, «Look at the weirdo», and points at a new girl eating alone. Why is this unkind? | *It is a rude label that can hurt someone | It is a joke that everyone laughs at | It is the same as a friendly hug | It means she is a famous cook
test: Which use of weirdo is friendly? | *Said laughing to a friend who did something silly | Written in a formal letter to the head teacher | Shouted at a dog | Said quietly to a stranger who is sitting still
test: Weirdo is a slang word. What does slang mean? | *Informal words used in casual talk | A very old word from the Bible | A word only teachers are allowed to use | A type of food from another country
exam: A story says, «He called her a weirdo and turned his back.» What does this show about how he sees her? | He is laughing with her at a silly joke | *He thinks she is odd and does not want to be her friend | He is asking her to play a game | He thinks she is the best person he knows
